    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50165" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vānĭtĭes</span></b> ,
		ēï, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>emptiness</i>, <i>nullity</i>, <i>folly</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plebeia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 1, 13</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., <i>vanity</i>, <i>vainglory</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad extollendam ejus vanitiem sidera quoque, si
					jussisset, exhiberi posse promittens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 1, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
